# 🔟 Key Takeaways

1. **Attention is a limited resource.**
2. **Productivity is strongly connected to attention management.**
3. **Multitasking can fragment your attention.**
4. **Choose what deserves your attention before beginning.**
5. **Remove distractions instead of relying only on willpower.**
6. **Hyperfocus helps execution.**
7. **Scatterfocus helps creativity and connection-making.**
8. **Breaks can be productive when intentional.**
9. **More working hours don't automatically mean more valuable output.**
10. **Learn to control your attention instead of allowing everything around you to control it.**

